\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Come, let us to the Lord our God
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  With contrite hearts return;
\par  Our God is gracious, nor will leave
\par  The desolate to mourn.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  His voice commands the tempest forth,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj  And stills the stormy wave;
\par  And though His arm be strong to smite,
\par  'tis also strong to save.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Long hath the night of sorrow reigned,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  The dawn shall bring us light:
\par  God shall appear, and we shall rise
\par  With gladness in His sight.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li405\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.   Our hearts, if God we seek to know,
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0 Shall know Him, and rejoice;
\par His coming like the morn shall be,
\par Like morning songs His voice.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li405\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.   As dew upon the tender herb,
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0 Diffusing fragrance round;
\par As showers that usher in the spring,
\par And cheer the thirsty ground:
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li405\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  So shall His presence bless our souls
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0 And shed a joyful light;
\par That hallowed morn shall chase away
\par \pard       The sorrows of the night.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

